    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test \u2014 the only test class). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date, responding **400**, following the existing OfficeFloor function-injection patterns in the codebase.\n\nNew files:\n- **`RejectFutureRegistrationDate.java`** \u2014 a single-responsibility step that reads the already-published `OwnerFieldsDto`, accepts requests that omit the date, and throws `FutureRegistrationDateException` when the supplied date is after `LocalDate.now()`. Mirrors the structure of the existing `Reject*` steps.\n- **`FutureRegistrationDateException.java`** \u2014 checked exception (extends `Exception`) so it surfaces in a `throws` clause.\n- **`FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 responds 400 via `ProblemDetails.build`, identical to `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler`.\n- **`...FutureRegistrationDateException.yml`** \u2014 escalation wiring for the handler.\n\nWiring:\n- Inserted `rejectFutureRegistrationDate` into `owners.POST.yml` **after** postcode validation and **before** `resolveRegistrationDate` \u2014 so the raw supplied date is checked before any business-day roll-forward adjusts it.\n\nI placed the future-date check in its own step rather than folding it into `ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate` (which resolves/rolls the date) to keep each class to a single responsibility. The targeted acceptance test and the full suite both pass.",
